# TOUCH — stroking the big pet in its panel. Both frames derive from react.pet 'happy'.
# Head and shoulders (rows 0-10) lean 1 px into the stroking hand, the head tilting with it
# (the ear on the hand's side drops 1 row). ^ ^ eyes, p blush on row 7, p mouth as happy.
# Feet, haunches and tail base (rows 13-15) are happy's. The tail tip is idle 'sit_tail_1'
# (1 row lower than happy) in BOTH frames: with happy's tail, lean_right's cheek sat on the
# tail tip; this gives the head room and keeps the tail identical between the two leans.
# lean_right is lean_left mirrored about the fox's centre line (boundary x=7, col c <-> 13-c),
# except the tail, which stays on the right.

@frame lean_left
